<title>HONG KONG: HK bourse member to face bribery trial on April 21.</title>
<headline>HK bourse member to face bribery trial on April 21.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A council member of the Hong Kong Stock Exchange, Chen Po-sum, will face trial on April 21 on bribery charges, the local anti-graft watchdog Independent Commission Against Corruption (ICAC) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Chen, 66, is charged with soliciting HK$1.5 million and accepting HK$1.6 million in connection with the transfer of seats at the exchange, the ICAC said in a statement.</p>
<p>The coming trial will take place at the High Court, it said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
